WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.190
A decoder converts an encoded input into an active output line.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:10.665
In an ideal active-high 2-to-4 decoder, each two-bit input selects exactly one of four outputs when enabled.

00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:16.760
Real devices may use active-low outputs or additional enable pins, so read the chosen device’s datasheet.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.613
Y2 is 1 in the active-high enabled model; Y0, Y1 and Y3 are 0.

00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:26.080
This is a one-hot representation of the input value 2.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.136
In the stated model, input 11 activates which output?

00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:33.840
Binary 11 selects output number 3.
